From: PS5_Proton
Subject: [PATCH] user32: refresh receiver caches before shared appearance notifications

An existing PE32 or PE64 process receives WM_THEMECHANGED but continues to
report and open its previous theme. Its cached system colours also survive
WM_SYSCOLORCHANGE. Refresh the local theme file through the existing USER
hook before application dispatch, without writing registry state or metrics.
Invalidate local colour values and cached GDI objects at the common receiver
boundary. Old HTHEME references remain valid until their owners close them.

The paired cross-process probe reproduces three failed assertions in each
architecture on the preceding runtime: theme name, pane colour and new theme
caption colour. This changes shared Wine behavior without title conditions.

--- a/include/winuser.h
+++ b/include/winuser.h
@@ -4874,6 +4874,7 @@
